1
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,103
He is hungry.

2
00:00:08,203 --> 00:00:12,441
It's fast and weighs almost a ton,

3
00:00:12,541 --> 00:00:16,678
(music)

4
00:00:16,778 --> 00:00:20,582
but it is not the only giant predator at the shark center.

5
00:00:20,682 --> 00:00:26,588
(music)

6
00:00:26,688 --> 00:00:31,393
More large shark species live here than anywhere else on the planet.

7
00:00:31,493 --> 00:00:51,746
(music)

8
00:00:51,847 --> 00:00:53,682
They all share a current.

9
00:00:53,782 --> 00:00:56,818
(music)

10
00:00:56,919 --> 00:01:03,225
A vital sigh that joins a perfect shark storm.

11
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:07,496
Shark Rules.

12
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:21,776
The great white shark is the largest cold water predator, but also a world traveler,

13
00:01:21,876 --> 00:01:25,046
and this male is about to begin an epic journey.

14
00:01:26,715 --> 00:01:33,288
He is ready to leave when a sudden current of cold water diverts his course to a place

15
00:01:33,388 --> 00:01:35,057
distant hunting.

16
00:01:41,263 --> 00:01:47,870
Clouds of crustaceans accumulate in cold places.

17
00:01:51,974 --> 00:01:57,480
He needs food before he leaves, but crustaceans are not in his diet.

18
00:02:00,082 --> 00:02:02,017
Chase a trail.

19
00:02:02,818 --> 00:02:04,420
Something in the distance.

20
00:02:08,423 --> 00:02:11,894
Something that is at the other end of the food chain.

21
00:02:11,994 --> 00:02:17,666
The enormous humpback whales.

22
00:02:17,766 --> 00:02:33,349
(music)

23
00:02:33,449 --> 00:02:37,552
Whales gather to eat the crustaceans brought by the current.

24
00:02:37,652 --> 00:02:49,031
(music)

25
00:02:49,131 --> 00:02:51,099
The biggest ones eat the small ones,

26
00:02:51,199 --> 00:03:02,144
(music)

27
00:03:02,244 --> 00:03:05,414
but this shark has an insatiable appetite

28
00:03:05,514 --> 00:03:20,795
(music)

29
00:03:20,895 --> 00:03:23,332
and giants are not invincible.

30
00:03:28,771 --> 00:03:35,077
This is what the great white shark perceives.

31
00:03:35,177 --> 00:03:39,081
Even dead, the whale moves with the current.

32
00:03:40,883 --> 00:03:48,123
The smell of rotting fat that it gives off is like a drug to the great white shark.

33
00:03:48,223 --> 00:04:16,485
(music)

34
00:04:16,585 --> 00:04:21,257
Before a long journey, a great white shark must sate itself with food.

35
00:04:23,458 --> 00:04:27,529
He needs all the energy he can get for the journey ahead.

36
00:04:27,629 --> 00:04:35,003
(music)

37
00:04:35,103 --> 00:04:39,674
Despite its size, you must be alert to danger.

38
00:04:39,775 --> 00:04:45,047
There will always be someone bigger

39
00:04:45,147 --> 00:04:50,218
and this species has not survived 11 million years because it is naive.

40
00:04:50,318 --> 00:04:55,490
(music)

41
00:04:55,590 --> 00:04:59,295
The dead whale is a good farewell gift before the journey.

42
00:05:02,131 --> 00:05:05,167
And it's designed to eat this.

43
00:05:15,710 --> 00:05:22,251
It has triangular teeth in a springy jaw made for holding and slicing.

44
00:05:36,231 --> 00:05:39,568
He can't bite for long.

45
00:05:39,668 --> 00:05:41,403
You need to move to breathe,

46
00:05:49,478 --> 00:05:53,415
but the more he eats, the greater his appetite.

47
00:06:17,005 --> 00:06:33,155
(music)

48
00:06:33,255 --> 00:06:36,958
The great white shark is famous for its binge eating.

49
00:06:37,058 --> 00:06:40,295
If there is food, he takes it.

50
00:06:40,395 --> 00:07:03,184
(music)

51
00:07:03,285 --> 00:07:08,190
The pieces of fat are converted into energy that is stored in your large liver.

52
00:07:13,728 --> 00:07:15,564
His movements are almost...

53
00:07:15,664 --> 00:07:17,132
mechanics.

54
00:07:17,232 --> 00:07:51,699
(music)

55
00:07:51,799 --> 00:07:57,505
His stomach is full of fat, the fuel that will take him to a distant shore called

56
00:07:57,605 --> 00:07:59,608
shark center.

57
00:08:08,049 --> 00:08:13,522
It's a 1,400-kilometer journey from where you are at the tip of Africa,

58
00:08:13,622 --> 00:08:19,828
where two streams meet: one cold and rich with nutrients,

59
00:08:19,928 --> 00:08:22,231
and the other warm and comforting.

60
00:08:25,933 --> 00:08:31,173
Once a year, the cold current reaches the coast and a countercurrent is created.

61
00:08:33,441 --> 00:08:36,678
The great white shark will travel on it to a unique meeting

62
00:08:36,778 --> 00:08:40,549
where an incredible mix of sea hunters awaits.

63
00:08:43,017 --> 00:08:49,191
He knows exactly where he's going and will need to feed himself along the way.

64
00:08:53,828 --> 00:08:57,032
The next stop is the kelp beds.

65
00:08:58,734 --> 00:09:04,306
There is plenty of prey here.

66
00:09:04,406 --> 00:09:10,012
Young sea lions are snacks for a shark.

67
00:09:14,549 --> 00:09:18,452
His island castle has a seaweed moat.

68
00:09:18,553 --> 00:09:26,327
A security fence included that for a sea lion it is...

69
00:09:26,427 --> 00:09:28,129
like a playground.

70
00:09:28,229 --> 00:09:47,949
(music)

71
00:09:48,049 --> 00:09:51,086
New puppies are arriving right now.

72
00:10:01,529 --> 00:10:06,168
All of them beautiful, tender and defenseless,

73
00:10:10,772 --> 00:10:16,979
But for a great white shark they are delicious little bites.

74
00:10:37,298 --> 00:10:38,800
Maybe they are safe on the island,

75
00:10:43,905 --> 00:10:47,742
But there is something that the white shark knows very well,

76
00:10:47,843 --> 00:10:50,145
the coast is certain death.

77
00:10:54,416 --> 00:10:58,920
If any little one wants to feed, he will have to leave the fortress.

78
00:11:03,658 --> 00:11:04,960
sooner or later.

79
00:11:16,037 --> 00:11:22,678
Leaving the island and the seaweed is not safe, but the seals must hunt far out to sea.

80
00:11:29,918 --> 00:11:34,756
And waiting just at the edge of the deep waters is the great white shark.

81
00:11:39,861 --> 00:11:44,566
The seals walk in groups at first, but eventually each one goes on its own.

82
00:11:47,835 --> 00:11:53,008
Seals are fast, but they're no match for a flying shark.

83
00:12:05,453 --> 00:12:06,788
It took them by surprise,

84
00:12:10,258 --> 00:12:11,493
awesome.

85
00:12:20,768 --> 00:12:22,871
At first it stays down,

86
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:27,976
crawling deep,

87
00:12:30,478 --> 00:12:31,947
look up

88
00:12:35,249 --> 00:12:38,553
and chases the silhouettes.

89
00:12:38,653 --> 00:12:43,024
Incredibly, great white sharks can generate body heat.

90
00:12:43,124 --> 00:12:46,495
Even in icy waters, their engines are warm

91
00:12:49,097 --> 00:12:53,635
and ready to unleash extraordinary energy in a single burst.

92
00:12:55,670 --> 00:13:00,375
A special vein supplies the shark's brain with warm blood,

93
00:13:00,475 --> 00:13:05,213
So he's not just fast, he thinks fast.

94
00:13:08,316 --> 00:13:13,855
Relative to their size, sharks have some of the largest livers on the planet.

95
00:13:13,955 --> 00:13:20,161
and they not only serve as fuel containers, but they also give them dynamism

96
00:13:20,261 --> 00:13:25,033
and its high fat content gives them strength when they need it most.

97
00:13:43,285 --> 00:13:47,321
I can see you, but do you see me?

98
00:13:47,421 --> 00:14:07,575
(music)

99
00:14:07,675 --> 00:14:10,311
The timing must be perfect.

100
00:14:10,411 --> 00:14:12,213
Seals are fast.

101
00:14:12,313 --> 00:14:38,740
(music)

102
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:42,010
The prey has half the chance of escaping.

103
00:14:46,213 --> 00:14:47,716
This one was lucky.

104
00:14:48,950 --> 00:14:50,752
The next one maybe not so much.

105
00:15:12,107 --> 00:15:14,442
It's time to leave them alone.

106
00:15:16,511 --> 00:15:21,016
The journey awaits and the current presses.

107
00:15:23,518 --> 00:15:26,154
Ahead, the flow is heading towards the coast,

108
00:15:26,254 --> 00:15:29,424
where it collides with the warm current of the Indian Ocean.

109
00:15:31,459 --> 00:15:34,062
The shark station is up ahead.

110
00:15:36,965 --> 00:15:43,204
The current changes rhythm and begins to churn, mixing cold water with warm water.

111
00:15:44,205 --> 00:15:50,245
Every eddy and pulse drives the feast toward the shore, uniting species from temperate waters

112
00:15:50,345 --> 00:15:51,913
and tropical.

113
00:15:53,281 --> 00:15:56,851
The current extends about 160 kilometers.

114
00:15:56,951 --> 00:16:00,889
A place with a shark population like almost no other.

115
00:16:02,624 --> 00:16:08,763
Cold water fish gather in the current, safe and slippery

116
00:16:08,863 --> 00:16:12,100
and migrate to the tropics to spawn.

117
00:16:13,234 --> 00:16:17,872
Tons of food on the move.

118
00:16:17,972 --> 00:16:19,874
The current hypnotizes them.

119
00:16:23,511 --> 00:16:25,780
This is why the great white shark is here

120
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:30,818
(music)

121
00:16:30,919 --> 00:16:32,854
and even seals follow him.

122
00:16:36,424 --> 00:16:39,561
These clouds of fish are the big attraction.

123
00:16:41,929 --> 00:16:46,835
More great white sharks bring up the rear, but other species await ahead.

124
00:16:50,038 --> 00:16:53,441
A mix of predators moves in to corner the fish

125
00:16:57,979 --> 00:17:00,915
and collides with the newly arrived sharks.

126
00:17:02,683 --> 00:17:10,458
Bull sharks, sand sharks and several of these.

127
00:17:10,558 --> 00:17:12,127
The black tips.

128
00:17:14,562 --> 00:17:18,566
This day hunter is aerodynamic and fast

129
00:17:22,703 --> 00:17:25,740
and grows up to 2.5 meters.

130
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:29,677
A giant, if you're a 4-inch mackerel.

131
00:17:32,446 --> 00:17:39,320
Blacktips travel with the current and approach the coast,

132
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:44,159
preparing to enjoy the feast that awaits there.

133
00:17:50,498 --> 00:17:52,299
They have little hope.

134
00:17:52,399 --> 00:17:55,370
Sharks surround the giant ball of prey.

135
00:17:57,372 --> 00:18:02,877
Blacktips hunt along the banks, forcing small fish to congregate.

136
00:18:05,045 --> 00:18:10,752
A blacktip swishes its tail to reach speeds of up to 22 kilometers per hour.

137
00:18:10,852 --> 00:18:14,021
Its snout opens almost 90 degrees.

138
00:18:14,121 --> 00:18:15,723
A big breath.

139
00:18:15,823 --> 00:18:34,408
(music)

140
00:18:34,508 --> 00:18:36,610
At first the group is large,

141
00:18:36,710 --> 00:18:49,757
(music)

142
00:18:49,857 --> 00:18:51,392
then it decreases

143
00:18:51,492 --> 00:18:59,400
(music)

144
00:18:59,501 --> 00:19:00,468
more and more

145
00:19:00,568 --> 00:19:11,579
(music)

146
00:19:11,679 --> 00:19:13,381
until it disappears.

147
00:19:24,492 --> 00:19:26,761
The environment is left clean.

148
00:19:57,692 --> 00:20:03,698
Now the current crashes against the coast and heads towards the shark farm.

149
00:20:08,937 --> 00:20:13,775
Just 4 meters from the coast the waters reach a huge reef system

150
00:20:13,875 --> 00:20:15,609
plagued by other giants.

151
00:20:15,709 --> 00:20:22,183
(music)

152
00:20:22,283 --> 00:20:26,854
It is a junction of currents, one day warm, the next cold.

153
00:20:26,954 --> 00:20:28,789
(music)

154
00:20:28,889 --> 00:20:30,658
A melting pot of sharks.

155
00:20:30,758 --> 00:20:32,427
(music)

156
00:20:32,527 --> 00:20:36,297
There are more species here than anywhere else on the planet.

157
00:20:39,233 --> 00:20:47,040
It is the kingdom of elasmobranchs, fish with cartilaginous skeletons,

158
00:20:47,141 --> 00:20:50,678
sharks, rays and the like.

159
00:20:50,778 --> 00:21:02,289
(music)

160
00:21:02,390 --> 00:21:04,158
During the day it is a beautiful aquarium,

161
00:21:04,258 --> 00:21:12,199
(music)

162
00:21:12,299 --> 00:21:19,374
but the darkness reveals an underworld and a timid giant.

163
00:21:35,690 --> 00:21:38,926
One by one they emerge from the caves and grottos.

164
00:21:43,330 --> 00:21:46,234
Bull sharks are on the prowl.

165
00:21:50,972 --> 00:21:57,645
There may be thousands of sharks here, but bull sharks dominate the reef niches.

166
00:22:06,020 --> 00:22:10,958
At almost twice the length of a man, this is a gathering of giants.

167
00:22:29,643 --> 00:22:32,880
Unlike blacktips and whitetips,

168
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:35,650
Bulls do not need to swim to breathe.

169
00:22:42,590 --> 00:22:47,362
They pump water into their gills as they stalk.

170
00:22:52,165 --> 00:22:56,604
They appear lethargic, but can be extremely fast.

171
00:23:03,277 --> 00:23:09,717
While great white sharks cut with their teeth, bull sharks tear and rip with theirs,

172
00:23:14,021 --> 00:23:16,290
and are eager to use them.

173
00:23:21,362 --> 00:23:24,132
The bull shark has some secrets.

174
00:23:28,469 --> 00:23:31,372
This is a couples date night.

175
00:23:33,508 --> 00:23:35,743
The scars prove it.

176
00:23:37,812 --> 00:23:42,116
The female shows teeth marks from the males who held her.

177
00:23:43,350 --> 00:23:46,387
But mating whets the appetite.

178
00:23:48,255 --> 00:23:52,860
Its needle-like teeth do not slice, but pierce.

179
00:24:00,834 --> 00:24:05,272
His eyes are tiny, so he uses his electromagnetic sense

180
00:24:05,372 --> 00:24:07,241
to find food.

181
00:24:11,078 --> 00:24:16,551
The black spots on its head are gel sacs that detect vibrations from other fish.

182
00:24:19,587 --> 00:24:22,557
If your heart beats, there is no escape.

183
00:24:37,905 --> 00:24:44,145
Flatfish like sole are practically invisible,

184
00:24:44,245 --> 00:24:46,947
but she is an expert at finding them.

185
00:24:47,047 --> 00:25:42,336
(music)

186
00:25:42,436 --> 00:25:49,510
It's not just sharks that the current brings with it.

187
00:25:49,610 --> 00:25:53,748
This old male sea turtle is also an ocean traveler.

188
00:25:58,585 --> 00:26:05,126
He swam south from tropical waters and is exhausted from all the mating.

189
00:26:08,195 --> 00:26:12,466
His work is done, but he needs to regain his energy soon.

190
00:26:15,835 --> 00:26:21,074
Its shell is its only protection and for most predators

191
00:26:21,174 --> 00:26:26,914
It is impenetrable, but a majority does not mean "all."

192
00:26:31,685 --> 00:26:34,688
A tiger shark.

193
00:26:34,788 --> 00:26:39,860
If the great white shark is the giant of the south, he is the giant of the north.

194
00:26:43,631 --> 00:26:46,300
It is twice as long as a king-size bed,

195
00:26:46,400 --> 00:26:51,538
(music)

196
00:26:51,638 --> 00:26:56,077
and he is a hunter, a scavenger, and a garbage container.

197
00:26:59,180 --> 00:27:04,852
Tigers have one of the most acidic stomachs in the animal kingdom.

198
00:27:04,952 --> 00:27:09,957
From beer bottles to explosives, they are known for eating everything.

199
00:27:14,161 --> 00:27:16,097
He is also traveling.

200
00:27:20,367 --> 00:27:24,405
Tiger sharks can travel 1,100 kilometers in a month.

201
00:27:27,274 --> 00:27:30,177
This one travels from the tropical waters of the south...

202
00:27:30,277 --> 00:27:31,645
to hunt.

203
00:27:31,745 --> 00:27:41,588
(music)

204
00:27:41,688 --> 00:27:45,192
His navigation skills are impeccable.

205
00:27:46,159 --> 00:27:47,161
Get to know this reef.

206
00:27:51,999 --> 00:27:54,969
He comes here every year...

207
00:27:55,069 --> 00:27:56,303
for food.

208
00:28:03,110 --> 00:28:10,751
It is no coincidence that the turtle is the most sought after, alive or dead.

209
00:28:10,851 --> 00:28:28,769
(music)

210
00:28:28,869 --> 00:28:35,175
The exhausted sea turtle comes up for air,

211
00:28:35,275 --> 00:28:38,879
but it stays up longer than it should.

212
00:28:51,925 --> 00:28:54,762
The old turtle served his kind well

213
00:28:57,931 --> 00:29:00,300
and is now part of the cycle of life.

214
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:05,872
(music)

215
00:29:05,972 --> 00:29:08,542
The jaws of the tiger are wide and short

216
00:29:08,642 --> 00:29:12,679
(music)

217
00:29:12,780 --> 00:29:17,451
and combined with a powerful jaw can easily pierce through bone.

218
00:29:29,997 --> 00:29:33,200
And divides the portions of his food precisely.

219
00:29:33,300 --> 00:30:09,703
(music)

220
00:30:09,803 --> 00:30:13,640
The 220-kilogram turtle looks like a rag doll.

221
00:30:13,741 --> 00:30:16,309
under the awesome power of the shark.

222
00:30:16,409 --> 00:30:41,535
(music)

223
00:30:48,308 --> 00:30:55,148
Its unique teeth work like a heavy-duty can opener.

224
00:30:55,248 --> 00:30:58,151
and the shark extracts the proteins from inside.

225
00:30:58,251 --> 00:31:12,565
(music)

226
00:31:12,666 --> 00:31:16,937
Tiger sharks are truly successful predators.

227
00:31:19,205 --> 00:31:23,377
At the end of its hunting trip, the shark returns north.

228
00:31:25,112 --> 00:31:29,049
You must reach the tropics, where the water is warm and comforting.

229
00:31:30,284 --> 00:31:38,558
That's where it will reproduce in spring, where the backwash dissipates.

230
00:31:38,658 --> 00:31:44,064
While cruising through the shark farm, you pass someone else's hatchery.

231
00:31:49,769 --> 00:31:51,639
The mouth of the river.

232
00:31:58,212 --> 00:32:02,483
Fresh water flows into the ocean, warming the current.

233
00:32:06,253 --> 00:32:11,458
This special mix of fresh and salt water is a nursery for millions of fish,

234
00:32:17,063 --> 00:32:21,735
although just upstream lurks a real river monster.

235
00:32:24,471 --> 00:32:29,543
Rarely seen, but one of the most dangerous sharks in the world.

236
00:32:31,144 --> 00:32:32,913
The sardine shark.

237
00:32:39,553 --> 00:32:45,793
This is where he spends a lot of time, close to humans.

238
00:32:52,165 --> 00:32:58,172
It is the only shark adapted to survive in fresh water indefinitely.

239
00:33:01,441 --> 00:33:04,411
This female swims upriver to mate.

240
00:33:10,150 --> 00:33:12,953
Despite the murky color of the mud-laden water,

241
00:33:18,358 --> 00:33:22,596
will give birth to her young kilometers upriver in this estuary.

242
00:33:24,531 --> 00:33:28,568
Bull sharks can spend months in freshwater systems.

243
00:33:28,668 --> 00:33:32,039
and have been found more than 3 thousand kilometers in the river.

244
00:33:34,307 --> 00:33:41,781
Here you will live with the people, for whom, without knowing it,

245
00:33:41,881 --> 00:33:46,520
making your daily routine potentially life-threatening.

246
00:33:52,692 --> 00:33:56,329
The excellent hearing and sense of smell of the bull shark

247
00:33:56,429 --> 00:33:59,666
compensate for the reduced vision in such dirty waters.

248
00:34:07,941 --> 00:34:16,417
She is an expert hunter in the river and also in the ocean.

249
00:34:20,987 --> 00:34:27,995
Bull sharks are famous for their short, blunt snouts and aggressive nature.

250
00:34:31,131 --> 00:34:34,101
They are excellent predators in the open sea.

251
00:34:36,903 --> 00:34:42,643
The diminished current leads them to the northern limits of the shark center.

252
00:34:42,743 --> 00:34:48,615
The great sharks of the tropics converge here.

253
00:34:48,715 --> 00:34:51,751
Blacktips are also hunting here.

254
00:34:52,518 --> 00:34:56,757
The great masses of dams are a distant memory.

255
00:34:57,758 --> 00:35:01,328
As spring approaches, they look for an opportunity,

256
00:35:01,428 --> 00:35:03,730
or take advantage of other people's waste.

257
00:35:06,867 --> 00:35:10,503
This is also the territory of silvertip sharks.

258
00:35:10,603 --> 00:35:12,573
and hammerhead sharks.

